// S441 re-verification — item 19 (existing gaps g-spec-43-5-1-cross-program-rpc-example-is-invalid-scrml and
// g-spec-2-4-and-43-5-1-restatements-owed). SPEC §43.5.1's worked example, verbatim.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch); SPEC.md §43.5.1 at ~L26050
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/spec-43-5-1-await-example.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: the SPEC example compiles (dpa-056 R7 ruled §43.5.1 restated to return T, compiler-awaited).
// Actual:   §43.5.1 still reads `${ const result = await <#compute>.add(1, 2) }` and "Cross-program calls
//           return `Promise<T>`. Unawaited cross-program calls SHALL be compile error E-PROG-004." — the R7
//           restatement has not been written. Compiling it fires E-AWAIT-NOT-IN-SCRML (§19.9.8).
<program>
<program name="compute">
    ${ export function add(a: number, b: number) -> number { return a + b } }
</>
${ const result = await <#compute>.add(1, 2) }
</program>
